  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="935f9604-0e51-5028-a917-c7bfb8418d20" activityNameId="4c5b128d-0e5f-5c40-91c7-fbd193b4cbff" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Methylchloride, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Methylchloride, at plant
The data source for this process is a system inventory from Boustead. Due to the cumulated form of this data only the ressources and emissions included in the data source were considered. No land occupation and land use is included in this dataset. Further it was not possible to implement an uncertainity assessment with this data.;
CAS number: 000074-87-3; 
Formula: CH3Cl; 
Synonyms: monochloromethane, chloromethane; 
UUID: a86e40e4-1bf1-3124-8798-38c0e6b6af64
Raw materials, processing energy, emissions to air and water from process, energy services and transports, infrastructure only partly included, no infrastructure of main process included, no land use data included.
Location: Data from various plants within Europe.
Technology: Data refers to actual technology used in the companies included. This leads in total to an average value including all important production routes for this chemical
Time period: Time of literature publication. Measurements took place before this period.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data represent a large share of the European production. Due to the cummulated data source for the product system invetory there are important parameters as land use or soil emissions missing in this dataset. Considered are only emissions stated in the original source of Boustead. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty for LCI results cannot be determined. Terefore uncertainity set to 1 which means no uncertainity is included
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_a86e40e4-1bf1-3124-8798-38c0e6b6af64.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="aba8870e-0b32-5d98-adad-d2d94f9e4cf0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
